Conditions:
Step 1: If line 12 `return [i, self.num_map[complement]]` is executed, then the `if` condition `(complement in self.num_map and self.num_map[complement] != i)` in line 11 should be true.
Step 2: If condition `complement in self.num_map` is true, at least one `target - nums[i]` in line 10 equals an element in `nums`, which means there exists two elements in `nums` that their sum is equal to `target`.
Step 3: If condition `self.num_map[complement] != i` is true, then `self.num_map[target - nums[i]] != i`, meaning that the index of `target - nums[i]` is not equal to `i`.
